--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is PUBLIC, which means its source code can be read. It does NOT
mean the code may be reused.

Public visibility does not grant a licence. Absent a licence granting rights, the
default position applies: you may read this code, and you may not copy it, modify
it, redistribute it, or use it commercially.

Specifically, no permission is granted to:

  - copy, reproduce or mirror the source, in whole or in part;
  - create derivative works, forks or ports;
  - redistribute or sublicense, including in a bundle, product or dataset;
  - use the code, in whole or in part, in a commercial product or service;
  - deploy, host or operate it as a service;
  - train machine-learning models on it.

The repository is public because the engineering record is worth being legible —
the architecture notes, the blind-evaluation methodology, and the corpus policy
are written to be read and learned from. Reading and learning are permitted.
Copying the implementation is not.

